                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:12.0000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><p>"Biopharmaceuticals" systematically introduces modern biological drugs, including recombinant hormones, cytokines, therapeutic antibodies, gene medicines and gene therapy, therapeutic vaccines, cancer immunotherapy and antibody-drug conjugates. The course covers their technological principles, preparation processes, and applications, analyzes current development status and challenges, and explores their broad prospects in precision medicine and the treatment of major diseases. It aims to equip students with core knowledge and frontier developments in the research, development, and translation of biopharmaceuticals.</p></font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
